+
+## Visit State and Retrieval
+
+A visit is in exactly one review state:
+
+- `clean`: a current revision exists and no unresolved revision set is open; or
+- `unresolved`: a current revision exists and an unresolved revision set is open.
+
+Current-state retrieval returns the complete current revision and the review state. An unresolved response also returns an unresolved-set ID and the candidate revision IDs so callers cannot mistake the current revision for an export-ready decision. The complete candidate payloads are available through a separate unresolved-revision retrieval operation intended for coordinator review.
+
+Revision-history retrieval returns immutable revisions and their parent links in server receipt order, together with resolution records. Receipt order is presentation metadata, not scientific precedence. Original worker revisions remain retrievable after resolution.
+
+## Coordinator Resolution
+
+A coordinator resolves one unresolved set by submitting its ID and the exact candidate revision IDs observed during review. The operation is rejected without changing visit state if the set is no longer open or its candidates have changed. This prevents a decision from silently excluding a submission that arrived during review.
+
+The coordinator records an outcome in one of two forms:
+
+- select one candidate revision unchanged as current; or
+- submit a complete replacement payload that creates a new resolution revision, used when the coordinator deliberately combines or corrects candidate content.
+
+Both forms create an immutable resolution record containing the coordinator ID, resolution time, reviewed candidate revision IDs, and selected revision ID. For a replacement, the new revision links to the previously current revision as its parent and to the resolution record as its provenance; the reviewed candidates remain independent immutable revisions rather than becoming field-level ancestors.
+
+Resolution atomically closes the unresolved set and makes the selected or replacement revision current. A replacement payload passes the same field and plot-reference validation as a worker submission. Resolution does not erase or rewrite any candidate.
+
+## Failure and Integrity Rules
+
+- An unknown visit, revision, or unresolved-set ID returns a not-found result without mutation.
+- A base revision from another visit, an invalid payload, or an idempotency-key mismatch returns a validation or conflict result without mutation.
+- Only authenticated workers may submit worker revisions, and only coordinators may resolve unresolved sets. Authentication and role assignment remain supplied by the team's identity provider.
+- Accepted submissions, revisions, and resolution records are immutable. Current pointers and review-state transitions are transactional derived state.
+
+## Downstream Contracts
+
+Tablet-sync must retain the base revision ID with each local edit, send complete visit payloads, and preserve an accepted unresolved outcome for later explanation to the worker. Its retry behavior uses the complete submission envelope and worker-scoped idempotency key defined here.
+
+Review-export must treat `unresolved` as distinct from the usable current payload, compare whole candidate revisions, and resolve against the exact candidate set it displayed. Export eligibility and coordinator presentation belong to review-export; it may not infer a winner or overwrite record-store history.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Concurrent edits | [Preserve complete competing revisions for coordinator resolution](decisions/concurrent-visit-edits.md) | Field-aware three-way merge | Whole revisions keep scientifically related fields in the context submitted by a worker and avoid silently combining edits whose relationship cannot be inferred from structure. The larger review queue is an accepted operating cost. |
+| Resolution output | Permit selection of a candidate or an explicit complete replacement revision | Candidate selection only; automatic field merge | Coordinators can retain useful content from more than one candidate without giving the server implicit scientific merge authority, while every resulting value remains attributable to a deliberate resolution. |
+| Review race handling | Resolve only the exact candidate set reviewed | Automatically include late candidates; lock out submissions during review | Exact-set comparison prevents silent omission without blocking field work while a coordinator has a review open. |
+
+## Open Questions & Future Decisions
+
+Tablet presentation, synchronization scheduling, coordinator comparison UI, export eligibility, and CSV construction belong to their downstream design nodes. The record-store contract does not depend on those choices.
